// AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/50_export_dashboard_data.py — do not edit by hand.
// Per (ticker, period_end), credit-quality metrics expressed as percent of
// amortized cost. All metrics are 0..100. Period_end is restricted to
// calendar quarter ends (3/31, 6/30, 9/30, 12/31).
//
// A special ticker = "industry" row aggregates across all 19 in-house BDCs
// PLUS the SEC DERA long-tail BDCs (~160 additional BDCs) for the
// mark-based metrics (pct_below_95 / pct_below_90 / pct_below_80). For
// non-accrual and PIK metrics, the industry row uses in-house data only
// (DERA bulk SOI extracts don't tag those reliably).
//
// Mark-based numerator/denominator both restrict to DEBT positions only —
// equity / warrants / JV / cash / unfunded-commitment rows are excluded
// because par_amount is either meaningless or stores share counts (which
// would generate spurious "below 90c" flags as fv$ / shares).
//
//   pct_non_accrual    non-accrual share of investment cost, excluding cash
//                      equivalents and unfunded commitments. na_basis says where
//                      it comes from: parsed_positive_cost_investments (decoded
//                      positions), issuer_disclosed_zero (the filing states nothing
//                      was on non-accrual), issuer_reported_rate /
//                      issuer_reported_total_investments (the issuer's own %).
//                      null = unknown, never a silent zero. n_positions = 0 marks a
//                      disclosure-only quarter with no accepted book (MFIC).
// Industry NA pools every BDC with a supported cost rate, weighted by its
// in-scope cost (na_eligible_cost_b); na_covered_bdcs of na_universe_bdcs BDCs
// with a book that quarter contribute.
//   pct_below_95       cost of debt positions where FV/par < 0.95 / debt cost
//   pct_below_90       cost of debt positions where FV/par < 0.90 / debt cost
//   pct_below_80       cost of debt positions where FV/par < 0.80 / debt cost
//   pct_pik_total      legacy numeric alias of pct_pik_total_lower
//   pct_pik_total_lower known-positive PIK cost / positive-cost approved snapshot
//   pct_pik_total_upper (known-positive + unknown applicable) cost / snapshot
// Observation coverage is observed / (observed + unknown) applicable cost;
// not_applicable positions are excluded from that coverage denominator.
//   pct_pik_minimal    cost of PIK-severity=minimal positions
//   pct_pik_moderate   cost of PIK-severity=moderate positions
//   pct_pik_severe     cost of PIK-severity=severe positions
// Severe PIK by TYPE (scripts/pik_origin.py) — the four add up to pct_pik_severe:
//   pct_pik_severe_by_design   preferred / equity / convertible notes: PIK
//                              built into the instrument
//   pct_pik_severe_first_seen  debt already PIK the first time it appears in
//                              our data (not necessarily at origination)
//   pct_pik_severe_switched    debt that paid cash while held, then switched to
//                              PIK (the stress signal)
//   pct_pik_severe_unknown     debt whose history cannot tell

